# Ownership of publication-sensitive files.
#
# IMPORTANT — this file documents ownership. It is deliberately NOT paired with
# a `require_code_owner_review: true` ruleset rule at present.
#
# GitHub does not let a pull-request author approve their own pull request. With
# a single eligible human reviewer, requiring code-owner approval would make
# every self-authored PR unmergeable, and the only way out would be an admin
# bypass — which would turn the routine path into the bypass path and destroy
# the control we are building. A gate that must be bypassed to do ordinary work
# is worse than no gate, because it normalises bypassing.
#
# The publication boundary is therefore enforced by:
#   1. a mandatory pull request for the default branch (no direct pushes);
#   2. required status checks that must pass before merge, including the
#      publication/hygiene gate;
#   3. the fail-closed canonical policy in assets/public_source_profile.json,
#      which rejects unknown and excluded paths mechanically.
#
# Machine gates do not get tired, and unlike a review requirement they cannot be
# satisfied by the author nodding at their own change.
#
# FUTURE HARDENING: if a genuinely independent human reviewer with write access
# ever joins the project, enable `require_code_owner_review: true` on the
# default-branch ruleset and set `required_approving_review_count` to 1. That is
# a strict improvement and should be done at that point, not before.

